From the k10–k12 review: cmd/launcher/main.go logs 'MCP server listening on …' right after starting go httpSrv.ListenAndServe(), before the port is bound. A client (or the launcher's own bridge smoke test, or a test) that acts on that line can hit 'connection refused'. TestRunRegistersTheSkillsToolWithTheLoadedSkills was flaky for this reason (17 of 40 with -count=40) and now retries. Fix: net.Listen first, log after it succeeds, then Serve(listener). A bind failure is then reported before the line too. Done: the line appears only when a request can connect, and a test pins it. Lane: unreagent-worker. main.go/run() card: run it serially.

